---
description: Sail-only shell conventions for Laravel / Docker commands.
alwaysApply: true
---

Always use the Sail binary at `/usr/local/bin/sail` for anything that touches the Laravel app, the database, the queue, the containers, or the JS toolchain. Do not rely on `$PATH` resolution.

Allowed:

- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail up -d`
- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail artisan migrate`
- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail npm run dev`
- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail bin pint`
- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail phpunit`
- `cd /-/reforged-spork && /usr/local/bin/sail phpunit tests/Feature/Foo/BarTest.php`

Disallowed:

- `./vendor/bin/sail …`
- bare `php artisan …` / bare `php …`
- `sail test` / `php artisan test` (the `test` alias does not work here — only `phpunit` does)

Always run from the project root `/-/reforged-spork`.
